'''''[[Strictly Come Dancing]]''''' returned for its '''seventeenth series''' with a launch show on 7 September 2019 on [[BBC One]], and the live shows beginning on 21 September. [[Tess Daly]] and [[Claudia Winkleman]] returned as hosts, while [[Zoe Ball]] returned to host ''[[Strictly Come Dancing: It Takes Two]]'' alongside new addition [[Rylan Clark]].<ref>{{cite web|title=BBC Blogs – Strictly Come Dancing – Rylan Clark-Neal joins Zoe Ball as the host of It Takes Two|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/webarchive/https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bbc.co.uk%2Fblogs%2Fstrictlycomedancing%2Fentries%2F04871464-b083-4094-8503-d8dd9e4d9723|publisher=BBC One|language=en|date=18 April 2019|access-date=18 April 2019}}</ref>

[[Shirley Ballas]], [[Craig Revel Horwood]], and [[Bruno Tonioli]] returned to the judging panel. After seven years, [[Darcey Bussell]] did not return to the series.<ref>{{cite web|title=BBC Blogs – Strictly Come Dancing – Dame Darcey Bussell decides to step down as judge from Strictly|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/webarchive/https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bbc.co.uk%2Fblogs%2Fstrictlycomedancing%2Fentries%2F6570af93-cd3a-46b0-955a-ff92a820d0e4|publisher=BBC One |language=en|date=10 April 2019|access-date=10 April 2019}}</ref> [[Motsi Mabuse]], elder sister of professional dancer [[Oti Mabuse]], was announced as Bussell's replacement on 22 July.<ref>{{cite web|title=BBC Blogs – Strictly Come Dancing – Welcome our new Strictly Judge Motsi Mabuse! |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/webarchive/https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bbc.co.uk%2Fblogs%2Fstrictlycomedancing%2Fentries%2Faec69db0-d4e1-4c65-bdec-a771d2c656b2|publisher=BBC One|language=en|date=22 July 2019|access-date=22 July 2019}}</ref> On 19 October, actor [[Alfonso Ribeiro]] returned as a guest judge.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.walesonline.co.uk/lifestyle/tv/alfonso-bruno-tonioli-strictly-dancing-17107747|title=Who is Alfonso Ribeiro? The judge replacing Bruno Tonioli on Strictly Come Dancing this week|last=Bevan|first=Nathan|website=[[Media Wales|Wales Online]]|language=en|date=18 October 2019|access-date=19 October 2019}}</ref>

''[[Emmerdale]]'' actor [[Kelvin Fletcher]] and Oti Mabuse were announced as the winners on 14 December, while ''[[EastEnders]]'' actress [[Emma Barton]] and [[Anton Du Beke]], and [[CBBC]] presenter [[Karim Zeroual]] and [[Amy Dowden]] were the runners-up.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/live/2019/dec/14/strictly-come-dancing-2019-the-final-live|title=Strictly Come Dancing 2019: the final – as it happened|work=[[The Guardian]]|first=Heidi|last=Stephens|date=14 December 2019|access-date=14 December 2019}}</ref>

