The couples dance each week in a live show. The judges score each performance out of ten. The couples are then ranked according to the judges' scores and given points according to their rank, with the lowest scored couple receiving one point, and the highest scored couple receiving the most points (the maximum number of points available depends on the number of couples remaining in the competition). The public are also invited to vote for their favourite couples, and the couples are ranked again according to the number of votes they receive, again receiving points; the couple with the fewest votes receiving one point, and the couple with the most votes receiving the most points.

The points for judges' score and public vote are then added together, and the two couples with the fewest points are placed in the bottom two. If two couples have equal points, the points from the public vote are given precedence. As with the previous series, the bottom two couples have to perform a dance-off on the results show. Based on that performance alone, each judge then votes on which couple should stay and which couple should leave, with [[Shirley Ballas]], as head judge, having the last and [[Casting vote|deciding vote]].

==Professional dancers==
On 1 March 2019, it was announced that [[Pasha Kovalev]] would be leaving the show after eight years as a professional dancer.<ref>{{cite web|title=BBC Blogs - Strictly Come Dancing - Our pro line-up for 2019 revealed!|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/webarchive/https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bbc.co.uk%2Fblogs%2Fstrictlycomedancing%2Fentries%2Fa0707981-d6f2-4f6f-8d4d-8b71678bcf01|publisher=BBC One|language=en|date=1 March 2019|access-date=1 March 2019}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.digitalspy.com/tv/reality-tv/a26319961/strictly-come-dancing-pasha-kovalev-quits-exit/|title=Strictly Come Dancing confirms one of its professional dancers has quit after eight series|last=Earp|first=Catherine|date=13 February 2018|work=[[Digital Spy]]|access-date=17 February 2018}}</ref> On 30 July 2019, [[Nancy Xu]] was revealed to have been added to the cast of professionals.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.bbc.com/news/entertainment-arts-49165516|title=Strictly Come Dancing: Nancy Xu named new professional dancer|website=[[BBC News]]|first=Paul|last=Glynn|date=30 July 2019|access-date=31 July 2019|language=en}}</ref> On 21 August 2019, it was confirmed that both [[Gorka Márquez]] and [[Graziano Di Prima]] would not have celebrity partners, a change from the previous series;<ref>{{cite web|title=Graziano di Prima will not get a celebrity partner this year|url=https://www.radiotimes.com/news/tv/2019-08-21/strictlys-graziano-di-prima-wont-have-a-celeb-partner-this-year/|website=Radio Times|access-date=21 August 2019}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.digitalspy.com/tv/reality-tv/a28775448/strictly-come-dancing-professional-gorka-marquez-demoted-no-celebrity-partner/|title=Strictly professional Gorka Marquez receives bad news about this year's series|website=Digital Spy|date=21 August 2019|access-date=21 August 2019}}</ref> in their place, the three professionals who did not have celebrity partners in series 16 - [[Neil Jones (dancer)|Neil Jones]], [[Johannes Radebe]], and [[Luba Mushtuk]] - were all given one for the first time.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.goodhousekeeping.com/uk/lifestyle/a28782378/strictly-come-dancing-neil-jones-johannes-radebe-partners/ |title=Strictly's Neil, Johannes and Luba get partners |last=Sutton |first=Megan |website=goodhousekeeping.com |date=9 September 2019 |access-date=22 September 2019}}</ref>

==Couples==
This series featured fifteen celebrity contestants. On 31 July 2019, the first three celebrities were announced: [[Emma Barton]], [[David James (footballer, born 1970)|David James]], and [[Chris Ramsey (comedian)|Chris Ramsey]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/webarchive/https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bbc.co.uk%2Fblogs%2Fstrictlycomedancing%2Fentries%2F6d7a6205-3329-4ad1-b007-2771b8e6492d|title=BBC Blogs – Strictly Come Dancing – Meet our first three stars of Strictly 2019|website=BBC One|date=31 July 2019|access-date=31 July 2019|language=en}}</ref> Celebrity reveals continued throughout the next week until the full line-up was revealed on 7 August 2019.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://metro.co.uk/2019/08/07/strictly-come-dancing-2019-full-line-michelle-visage-jamie-laing-10531995/|title=Meet the Strictly Come Dancing 2019 cast – from Michelle Visage to Jamie Laing|website=[[Metro (British newspaper)|Metro]]|first=Caroline|last=Westbrook|language=en|date=7 August 2019|access-date=7 August 2019}}</ref> ''[[Made in Chelsea]]'' star [[Jamie Laing]] was originally announced as a contestant, but on 5 September 2019, it was announced that he had withdrawn from the show due to a foot injury.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.mirror.co.uk/tv/tv-news/jamie-laing-quits-strictly-2019-19570153|title=Jamie Laing pulls out of Strictly Come Dancing after devastating injury|work=[[Daily Mirror]]|first1=Nicola|last1=Methven|first2=Emmeline|last2=Saunders|date=5 September 2019|access-date=5 September 2019|language=en}}</ref> He was replaced by former ''[[Emmerdale]]'' actor [[Kelvin Fletcher]] on 7 September 2019.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://metro.co.uk/2019/09/07/kelvin-fletcher-confirmed-to-replace-jamie-laing-on-strictly-come-dancing-2019-10704704/|title=Emmerdale's Kelvin Fletcher confirmed to replace Jamie Laing on Strictly Come Dancing 2019|work=[[Metro (British newspaper)|Metro]]|first=Adam|last=Starkey|date=7 September 2019|access-date=7 September 2019|language=en}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/webarchive/https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bbc.co.uk%2Fblogs%2Fstrictlycomedancing%2Fentries%2F3cf9fab3-fc24-48e0-be06-c4f706e9a531|title=BBC Blogs – Strictly Come Dancing – Say hello to your Strictly 2019 couples!|publisher=BBC One|date=7 September 2019|access-date=7 September 2019|language=en}}</ref>

Due to a knee injury sustained when he landed after jumping from a raised platform during studio rehearsals, [[Will Bayley]] was unable to perform on 26 October in the live episode. The injury was such that, on 30 October, he withdrew from the competition.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.bbc.com/news/entertainment-arts-50242471|title=Will Bayley leaves Strictly after leg injury|date=30 October 2019|via=www.bbc.co.uk}}</ref>
